# Dependency adoption review: `<package>`

Copy one file per proposed runtime dependency (development tools may share
one review per group). Replace every `<placeholder>`. Record the date and the
source URL for each piece of evidence so it can be re-checked.

## Request

| Field | Value |
| --- | --- |
| Package and ecosystem | `<name>` on `<PyPI, npm, ...>` |
| Exact index URL | `<https://pypi.org/project/name/>` |
| Proposed constraint | `<range for a library, exact version for an application>` |
| Dependency type | runtime / optional extra / development group |
| Requested by and date | `<handle>`, `<YYYY-MM-DD>` |
| Purpose | `<one sentence: what the code needs>` |

## Alternatives considered

| Option | Why not chosen |
| --- | --- |
| Standard library | `<reason>` |
| Existing dependency `<name>` | `<reason>` |
| Write and test locally | `<reason>` |

## Name and source verification

- [ ] Name copied from the project's own documentation or repository.
- [ ] Index page links to the repository and the repository links back.
- [ ] Near-miss names checked (separators, plurals, transpositions, prefixes).
- [ ] Not a brand-new package or a recent ownership transfer, or that risk is
      accepted below.
- [ ] Resolves from the intended index only (no shadowing internal name).

## Evidence

| Criterion | Evidence | Source and date | Meets hard limit |
| --- | --- | --- | --- |
| Maintenance | `<last release, open security issues>` | `<url, date>` | yes / no |
| Maintainers | `<people or organization with publish rights>` | `<url, date>` | yes / no |
| Release cadence | `<releases in the last year, changelog quality>` | `<url, date>` | yes / no |
| Adoption | `<dependents, download trend>` | `<url, date>` | context only |
| License | `<SPDX identifier>` | `<url, date>` | yes / no |
| Security posture | `<Scorecard score and failing checks; security policy; signed or attested releases>` | `<url, date>` | yes / no |
| Install-time code | `<wheels for all targets? lifecycle scripts?>` | `<url, date>` | yes / no |
| Transitive footprint | `<count and notable new packages>` | `<uv tree or npm ls output>` | yes / no |
| Known vulnerabilities | `<audit result for the proposed version>` | `<tool, version, date>` | yes / no |

## Decision

| Field | Value |
| --- | --- |
| Decision | approve / approve with conditions / reject |
